# Ownership for the knowledge-architecture library.
#
# STATUS: DORMANT AS ENFORCEMENT. CODEOWNERS is advisory text until branch
# protection makes owner review a required check (ai-kb:documents/decisions/0002-governance-without-enforcement.md).
# What it does today is answer one question: when a kb-audit sweep files a
# finding, who is it for? Without this file every finding reads `unassigned`,
# which is a queue nobody owns — the state in which a queue is ignored.
#
# The architecture asks for >=2 named owners per domain, so one departure does
# not orphan it. With a single contributor that is not satisfiable; it is
# recorded as an accepted risk rather than quietly dropped. Add the second owner
# before this library has real consumers.
#
# LAST MATCHING PATTERN WINS — not the most specific. Keep the broad rule first.
# `kb-owner <repo> <path>` resolves any path the way a sweep will.

